> has been baselined, not any semantic theory.
>

I'll wait for you to read the context then.


(I still don't know what a "cmevla" is.  I know what a "cmene" is)
>
>
A cmevla is any Lojban word that ends in a consonant.

Examples of (single) cmene that are not (single) cmevla are: "la'o gy
Starbucks gy", "la djan smit", "la selpa'i"

It is useful to be able to distinguish the special word form "cmevla" from
the more general notion of cmene. These two concepts used to be confused
when cmevla were called cmene, since not all cmene have the form of cmevla.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

